jp-protest/articleshow/134852234.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-10T16:07:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vivek Dubey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134852415,imgsize-1662820.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Muzzled Democracy': Congress slams government over mass detentions amid massive anti-SIR protests]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/muzzled-democracy-congress-slams-government-over-mass-detentions-amid-massive-anti-sir-protests/articleshow/134851226.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134851226.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Congress Party leaders have condemned the government's mass detentions during protests against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar in Delhi. They assert that numerous individuals, including activists and students, were detained while trying to voice dissent. The party emphasized the right to protest as essential to democracy and criticized the government for its heavy-handed approach.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/muzzled-democracy-congress-slams-government-over-mass-detentions-amid-massive-anti-sir-protests/articleshow/134851226.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/muzzled-democracy-congress-slams-government-over-mass-detentions-amid-massive-anti-sir-protests/articleshow/134851226.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-10T15:49:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134852015,imgsize-40606.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Can police arrest you for protesting? Know your rights and what happens next]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/protest-rights-in-india-when-can-police-stop-a-protest-or-detain-you/articleshow/134851835.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134851835.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The constitutional right to protest is fundamental, but it comes with responsibilities, allowing authorities to enforce regulations for the sake of public safety. Police may require permits for gatherings based on specific local laws, and they can issue dispersal orders when public safety is at risk, given legal justification. Detained individuals have the right to contest unlawful arrests and assert their rights through appropriate channels.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/protest-rights-in-india-when-can-police-stop-a-protest-or-detain-you/articleshow/134851835.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/protest-rights-in-india-when-can-police-stop-a-protest-or-detain-you/articleshow/134851835.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-10T15:48:14+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Saurabh Thakur</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134851949,imgsize-1797143.cms"/></item></channel></rss>